<title>AUSTRIA: Lamfalussy praises BOE's operational independence.</title>
<headline>Lamfalussy praises BOE's operational independence.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alexandre Lamfalussy, president of the European Monetary Institute, on Tuesday praised Britain's move to give the Bank of England greater operational independence and said it brought the country nearer Europe's monetary union criteria.</p>
<p>&quot;This is music to my ears. It is a very important decision. It goes quite a way towards meeting the requirements of the Maastricht Treaty,&quot; Lamfalussy told a conference organised by the Austrian National Bank. -- Vienna newsroom, +43-1 531 12 254</p>
</text>
